Passphrase file permissions and ownership:

#save the passphrase to the file
openssl rand -base64 32 >/etc/nginx/nginx_tls_passphrase.txt

chmod 600 /etc/nginx/nginx_tls_passphrase.txt
chown root:root /etc/nginx/nginx_tls_passphrase.txt

#since nginx runs under systemd, we can use systemd-creds for managing credentials that services can consume at runtime without the plaintext ever sitting persistently on disk or being readable via environment variable/process args:
 
systemd-creds encrypt /etc/pki/tls/private/nginx_tls_passphrase.txt /etc/pki/tls/private/nginx_tls_passphrase.cred

#encrypt using a key derived from the machine's own TPM 2.0 (if available) or a host-specific key stored in /var/lib/systemd/credential.secret
#.cred file can only be decrypted on the same machine, to enforce this behavior add:: --with-key=host
#rm /etc/pki/tls/private/nginx_tls_passphrase.txt
#nginx_identity.key's passphrase is automatically decrypted by systemd because it's declared in nginx's unit file via LoadCredntialEncrypted=nginx_pass:/etc/pki/tls/private/nginx_tls_passphrase.cred => every systemctl start nginx or restart runs, systemd decrypts it as part of the service startup sequence (only in-memory), so no manual systemd-creds decrypt invocation needed

##Encryption steps:
#systemd starts the nginx as root
#systemd reads /etc/pki/tls/private/nginx_tls_passphrase.cred (encrypted) -- root access
#systemd decrypts it in-memory using the machine's TPM2/host key
#systemd writes the decrypted plaintext to a runtime-only path: /run/credentials/nginx.service/nginx_tls_passphrase => plaintext, tmpfs, readable only by nginx's runtime user = root
#that runtime file is automatically to mode 0400 (in octal permissions)(r-- --- ---) owned by nginx service's actual runtime user which the OS-level User=root as specified on "ini" file:
----------------
ini 

[Service]
User=root
Group=root
#by default, it's root
----------------
#nginx via ssl_password_file points at that /run/credentials/... path, reads the now-plaintext file

#final step:
#systemctl daemon-reload
#systemctl restart nginx

